{
  "Version": 2,
  "Name": "Li2000-FTIR-PBS-IR-2",
  "Source": "L. Li and J. A. Dobrowolski, \"High-performance thin-film polarizing beam splitter operating at angles greater than the critical angle,\" Appl. Opt. 39, 2754-2771 (2000). doi:10.1364/AO.39.002754 - Table 3 (construction parameters); Table 2 (summary/performance); Fig. 4 (calculated performance)",
  "Notes": "Polarizing beam splitter operating above the critical angle (frustrated total internal reflection + interference), embedded between two prisms of n = 3.4: reflects p, transmits s\nSpecification: Rp ~ 1 and Ts ~ 1 (Rs, Tp -> 0) over 2-40 um (normalised wavenumber g = lambda0/lambda = 1.0-20.0, lambda0 = 40 um) for angles 54-70 deg in the prism (+/-28.2 deg in air)\nReported: extinction ratio > 3e3 in transmission, ~1e4 in reflection; Ts ~ 1, Rp ~ 1; total optical thickness 41.650 um; Fig. 4 plots Rs/Rp and Ts/Tp at 54, 62, 70 deg in the prism.\nNotes: Table 3 lists the layers from the substrate (prism) side, layer 1 adjacent to \"Sub.\"; the stack is symmetric (the table gives the first 41 layers and states that the remainder repeat them in reverse order, centre layer 41), and both bounding media are the same prism glass, so the order is the same from either side. Layers 42-81 expanded here from that rule. Indices are non-dispersive constants (n = 1.45 for odd layers, 4 for even layers), k = 0. Incident angle is in the prism (n = 3.4); the 'centre' angle used as angle_deg is the 0-deg-in-air angle of the Fig. 4 legend. Merit targets are my reading of the stated goal (Rp ~ 1, Ts ~ 1 over the band and angular field); the paper does not give its exact merit-function definition or sampling, so step_nm is my choice. Recomputed sum of n*d = 41649.94 nm vs Table 3 41650.19 nm.\nLayers from Table 3 (construction parameters); Table 2 (summary/performance); Fig. 4 (calculated performance); layer 1 faces the incident medium.\nChecked with ThinFilmDesigner (2026-10-21), agrees with the paper: ours optical thickness 41649.9 nm; over 2000-40000 nm at 62 deg: Ts >= 1.0000, Rp >= 1.0000, Ts/Tp >= 6.9e+4, Rp/Rs >= 3.0e+4; paper optical thickness 41650 nm; Ts/Tp > 3e+3, Rp/Rs ~1e+4.",
